    jit_struct_assignment_aliases_not_copies_2026-08-10, 2, "2026-11-10 root cause: Let/field-store arms copied value-struct PLACEs (copy_if_value_type) but HirStmt::Assign local re-assign (b = a), global assign, and rt_index_set (arr[i] = s) stored the aggregate handle directly, aliasing. Fix: lowering_stmt.rs applies copy_if_value_type (deep, classes excluded via type_value_kinds) at those three sites when the RHS is a place. Tests compiler/tests/compile_and_run.rs struct_reassign_copies_not_aliases, nested_struct_reassign_copies_inner, struct_stored_in_array_element_is_copied: red 3/4 -> green 5/5 (+struct_let_copy_field_mutate_keeps_source, class_reassign_keeps_reference_semantics control). Pre-existing unrelated reds: compile_preserves_root_import_types_for_annotated_local_fields, mir branch_coverage primitive_field_method_call_is_builtin_qualified."

